    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1798bcbc_13fef84b",
        "filename": "cc/library.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 875,
      "author": {
        "id": 1146974
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-12T05:51:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think so.\nIf the file name is not changed, other files cannot find this ext file.\nThis is to override the exiting VNDK file from the same-named file in `vendor/lib/vndk`.\nWith the VNDK deprecation, the vndk library can be updated directly without overriding. But still vndk-ext itself is defined to override the original file.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 874,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 875,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "95b6d8829b069ac750c542cd797bebb076be9fc8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4a942db8_b81cf0b3",
        "filename": "cc/library.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 875,
      "author": {
        "id": 1413436
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-12T08:29:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I also agonized a lot for this, but this won\u0027t be available once we remove all `vndk` properties from Android.bps anyway. I think the best way we can do is share a guideline to partners how to override former-vndk modules with vndk-ext. Probably we should try with `overrides: []` property, but need to test if this works as expected.",
      "parentUuid": "1798bcbc_13fef84b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 874,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 875,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "95b6d8829b069ac750c542cd797bebb076be9fc8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4194fce1_e341051e",
        "filename": "cc/library.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 875,
      "author": {
        "id": 1146974
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-12T10:32:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Once VNDK is totally removed, we don\u0027t need to support this override anymore. This is introduced to provide the way to modify the VNDK which cannot be changed directly. But with the VNDK deprecation, the extension is no longer required.\nUntil then, vndk-ext must override the pre-vndk library in /vendor/lib with the same libname. Otherwise, linker will ignore the vndk-ext that OEM originally wanted to load.",
      "parentUuid": "4a942db8_b81cf0b3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 874,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 875,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "95b6d8829b069ac750c542cd797bebb076be9fc8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "68af8eba_ee9afe62",
        "filename": "cc/library.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 875,
      "author": {
        "id": 1413436
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-15T03:51:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This change does not alter any behavior of VNDK-ext when VNDK version is defined. This is to (temporarily) handle case when VNDK is deprecated and VNDK-ext definition still exists.",
      "parentUuid": "4194fce1_e341051e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 874,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 875,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "95b6d8829b069ac750c542cd797bebb076be9fc8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e5d5d0eb_7d5294f7",
        "filename": "cc/library.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 875,
      "author": {
        "id": 1146974
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-15T04:57:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is the same with disabling the VNDK-ext libs because they may not be loaded after the VNDK deprecation. Any modules that has dependency on the VNDK-ext will fail on runtime without any build time detection.\n\nIf it is a temporary change until VNDK deprecation before 24Q2, it must include a TODO and must be fixed soon.",
      "parentUuid": "68af8eba_ee9afe62",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 874,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 875,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "95b6d8829b069ac750c542cd797bebb076be9fc8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0f1bf974_4bb342c4",
        "filename": "cc/library.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 875,
      "author": {
        "id": 1413436
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-15T05:56:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are right, but I cannot think of any good solution to solve this from Soong. I was planning to share partners manually override former VNDK libraries before VNDK is fully deprecated (with deprecation of BOARD_VNDK_VERSION). Please let me know if there is any other solutions.",
      "parentUuid": "e5d5d0eb_7d5294f7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 874,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 875,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "95b6d8829b069ac750c542cd797bebb076be9fc8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2772f3b8_21a6ffd2",
        "filename": "cc/library.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 875,
      "author": {
        "id": 1146974
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-15T06:41:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I prefer reporting correct error message on using vndk-ext with VNDK deprecation as there\u0027s no vndk libs to override.\nLess preferred option is to install the vndk-ext in `/vendor/lib/vndk` as before and search this path before searching `/vendor/lib` from the vendor namespace to override the existing pre-vndk lib in `/vendor/lib`.\n\nCurrent change is just hiding the errors from the build system.",
      "parentUuid": "0f1bf974_4bb342c4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 874,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 875,
        "endChar": 45
      },
